(7268816, 1131166, 30364, '<td valign="top">Lovely photograph, beautiful girl.  Welcome to my 7+ club.  Thank you.</td>', 'Lovely photograph, beautiful girl.  Welcome to my 7+ club.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 01:19:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268817, 1131123, 30364, '<td valign="top">Very interesting photograph of a nightmare.  Or possibly it''s a time machine.  In my 7+ picks, and thank you for offering something different.</td>', 'Very interesting photograph of a nightmare.  Or possibly it''s a time machine.  In my 7+ picks, and thank you for offering something different.', '2014-10-03 01:26:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268818, 1130328, 30364, '<td valign="top">Just like you, I love the preposterous street moments when ordinary people momentarily wear a silly costume.  Great chorus line in support makes this one all the more fun.  I think we all do these absurd things in public and never know it, because they''re only one heartbeat; the observer''s eye can''t see them unless it''s connected to a camera.  Into my 7+ selections.  Thank you.</td>', 'Just like you, I love the preposterous street moments when ordinary people momentarily wear a silly costume.  Great chorus line in support makes this one all the more fun.  I think we all do these absurd things in public and never know it, because they''re only one heartbeat; the observer''s eye can''t see them unless it''s connected to a camera.  Into my 7+ selections.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 01:33:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268820, 1131155, 30364, '<td valign="top">An uncomplicated idea beautifully realised.  The juxtaposition of that perfectly stilled human life with the blurred window scene is first among the several things I admire about this photograph.  And that''s the second: the <i>photograph</i> ... in spite of the striking pathos of the subject matter, the picture isn''t really about him, it''s about the photograph itself as a thing. We''re invited to reflect on what a photograph is, rather than simply what this man is. Well, I am so invited, and I hope a few others will be too.   Into my 7+ picks, and thank you.</td>', 'An uncomplicated idea beautifully realised.  The juxtaposition of that perfectly stilled human life with the blurred window scene is first among the several things I admire about this photograph.  And that''s the second: the photograph ... in spite of the striking pathos of the subject matter, the picture isn''t really about him, it''s about the photograph itself as a thing. We''re invited to reflect on what a photograph is, rather than simply what this man is. Well, I am so invited, and I hope a few others will be too.   Into my 7+ picks, and thank you.', '2014-10-03 01:49:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268821, 1130056, 30364, '<td valign="top">There''s only one DPC member with the ability to consistently make poetry from the scraps that others throw away, so if you aren''t John M then you are a disgraceful pretender and you may as well cease immediately because you''ll never last the course.  It''s a one man race I''m afraid.  It''s an automatic 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.</td>', 'There''s only one DPC member with the ability to consistently make poetry from the scraps that others throw away, so if you aren''t John M then you are a disgraceful pretender and you may as well cease immediately because you''ll never last the course.  It''s a one man race I''m afraid.  It''s an automatic 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 01:54:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268824, 1131157, 30364, '<td valign="top">Always love the transformative effect of the decisive crop.  It brings home the point that a really good photograph has life and meaning outside the frame.  If everything was inside the frame, this photograph would be less; surely even the dullest imagination can grasp that here?  It''s a clear 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.</td>', 'Always love the transformative effect of the decisive crop.  It brings home the point that a really good photograph has life and meaning outside the frame.  If everything was inside the frame, this photograph would be less; surely even the dullest imagination can grasp that here?  It''s a clear 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 02:04:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268831, 1130755, 30364, '<td valign="top">Lovely restraint in this photograph.  Well composed and beautifully rendered from a graphic point of view.  Alas it''s also cute enough to score really well, but hopefully it''s going to be appreciated for more than that, because it certainly has more to offer.  A 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.</td>', 'Lovely restraint in this photograph.  Well composed and beautifully rendered from a graphic point of view.  Alas it''s also cute enough to score really well, but hopefully it''s going to be appreciated for more than that, because it certainly has more to offer.  A 7+ pick for me.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 03:28:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268834, 1130336, 30364, '<td valign="top">A wonderful photograph.  As in <i>wonder-filled.</i> There are so many interesting qualities - and so many deft decisions made  for us to admire.  <br/> <br/>Perspective is one; either you''re very short, or you were smart enough to make yourself momentarily shorter to obtain the perfect (though slightly unnatural but the viewer doesn''t realise that) eye line through the scene.  It''s something that cinematographers do by instinct, but not so many still photographers do it, except for the great ones.  <br/> <br/>The decision (probably close to inevitable I admit, but worth comment anyway) to have part-vehicles both entering and exiting the frame on the two sides has bracketed the two girls in the most dynamic yet subtle way.  Had you waited, as a lesser eye might have done, for the sides to be ''distraction-free'', some of the intimacy of your photograph would be leaking away out of the sides.<br/> <br/>The fact that the two girls are looking together away from you, rather than facing you, also makes the photograph more interesting; more voyeuristic. That''s key to the charm of this picture; that it is a non-intrusive peek into a relationship.  It''s a non-confrontational street photographic, and all the better for that lightness of breath.<br/> <br/>The processing for a nostalgic, old-film effect is very often inappropriately deployed, but not here ... it''s just perfect for gently elevating the emotional essence of this picture.<br/> <br/>And then there''s all the things that played right into your hands without your intervention or decision: the timeless style of the modest dresses, the sensible walking shoes, and the holding hands.<br/> <br/>It''s a lovely, memorable, enviable photograph.  Please accept an Order of the Thumb, a 10, and a thank you for the picture.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'A wonderful photograph.  As in wonder-filled. There are so many interesting qualities - and so many deft decisions made  for us to admire.   Perspective is one; either you''re very short, or you were smart enough to make yourself momentarily shorter to obtain the perfect (though slightly unnatural but the viewer doesn''t realise that) eye line through the scene.  It''s something that cinematographers do by instinct, but not so many still photographers do it, except for the great ones.   The decision (probably close to inevitable I admit, but worth comment anyway) to have part-vehicles both entering and exiting the frame on the two sides has bracketed the two girls in the most dynamic yet subtle way.  Had you waited, as a lesser eye might have done, for the sides to be ''distraction-free'', some of the intimacy of your photograph would be leaking away out of the sides. The fact that the two girls are looking together away from you, rather than facing you, also makes the photograph more interesting; more voyeuristic. That''s key to the charm of this picture; that it is a non-intrusive peek into a relationship.  It''s a non-confrontational street photographic, and all the better for that lightness of breath. The processing for a nostalgic, old-film effect is very often inappropriately deployed, but not here ... it''s just perfect for gently elevating the emotional essence of this picture. And then there''s all the things that played right into your hands without your intervention or decision: the timeless style of the modest dresses, the sensible walking shoes, and the holding hands. It''s a lovely, memorable, enviable photograph.  Please accept an Order of the Thumb, a 10, and a thank you for the picture.', '2014-10-03 03:31:38.000000', NULL, 1),
